-- title:
--   Theorem 4.3, p. 237 — a semismooth, strongly BD-regular zero that is an accumulation point of the damped Newton method attracts the whole sequence superlinearly, and α_k eventually becomes 1
-- statement:
--   Let $F:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R^n$ be locally Lipschitz and B-differentiable at every point, and let $g=\tfrac12\|F\|^2$. Fix $\beta\in(0,1)$ and $\sigma\in(0,1/2)$, and let $\{x^k\}$ be any sequence generated by the damped Newton method (Algorithm 4.1) with $s=1$: $d^k$ solves $F(x^k)+F'(x^k;d^k)=0$, $\alpha_k=\beta^{m_k}$ with $m_k$ the first nonnegative integer passing the Armijo test (4.1), and $x^{k+1}=x^k+\alpha_k d^k$. Assume that $F(x^k)\ne0$ for all $k$.
--
--   Suppose $x^*$ is an accumulation point of $\{x^k\}$ and a zero of $F$, that $F$ is semismooth and strongly BD-regular at $x^*$, and that $F$ is semismooth on a neighbourhood of $x^*$. Then:
--   1. the entire sequence converges, $x^k\to x^*$;
--   2. the convergence is superlinear,
--   $$\|x^{k+1}-x^*\|=o(\|x^k-x^*\|)\qquad(k\to\infty);$$
--   3. $\alpha_k=1$ for all sufficiently large $k$.
--
--   The theorem answers three questions Pang raised about his damped Newton method for nonsmooth equations: whether the iteration converges to one point, at what rate, and when the step size becomes 1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Theorem 4.2 (b) holds" (each generalized Newton equation has a solution) is implied by the run hypothesis, which supplies a solution $d^k$ at every iterate. Global B-differentiability is the setting of Theorem 4.2, on which Algorithm 4.1's analysis rests. Semismoothness on a neighbourhood of $x^*$ is an added hypothesis inherited from Corollary 3.4, whose proof uses (2.16) at points near $x^*$; Lemma 2.6 proves (2.16) only at semismooth points. An accumulation point is a cluster point of the sequence ($\{x^k\}$ is frequently in every neighbourhood of $x^*$).
-- source:
--   Qi, Convergence analysis of some algorithms for solving nonsmooth equations, Math. Oper. Res. 18 (1993), p. 237, Theorem 4.3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QiNonsmoothEq_Damped_Setting

namespace QiNonsmoothEq.Damped

open Filter Topology NonsmoothNewton.Local NonsmoothNewton.Shared

theorem theorem_4_3 {n : ℕ} (F : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hF : LocallyLipschitz F) (hB : ∀ y, BDiffAt F y)
    (β σ : ℝ) (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hσ0 : 0 < σ) (hσ1 : σ < 1 / 2)
    (x d : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (α : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hrun : IsDampedNewtonRun F 1 β σ x d α) (hne : ∀ k, F (x k) ≠ 0)
    (xstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hclu : MapClusterPt xstar atTop x) (hzero : F xstar = 0)
    (hss : SemismoothAt F xstar) (hreg : StronglyBDRegularAt F xstar)
    (hssN : ∀ᶠ y in 𝓝 xstar, SemismoothAt F y) :
    Tendsto x atTop (𝓝 xstar) ∧
      (fun k => x (k + 1) - xstar) =o[atTop] (fun k => x k - xstar) ∧
      ∀ᶠ k in atTop, α k = 1 := by sorry

end QiNonsmoothEq.Damped
